AI usage disclosure: Generated with OpenAI's built-in imagegen tool.

Handle edit prompt (OpenAI built-in imagegen):
Use case: precise-object-edit. Asset type: existing pixel-art background for a Godot apple-dodging game. Input image: the supplied basket image is the edit target. Change only the basket handles. Remove the single large handle arch at the TOP and restore the plain dark olive background behind it. Add exactly TWO matching compact wicker loop handles, one at the middle of the LEFT outer side and one at the middle of the RIGHT outer side (9 o'clock and 3 o'clock). They should curve outward into the narrow outer margin and attach to the outside of the left/right rim, like the side grab handles of an apple-picking basket. Keep both handles completely visible inside the image. Keep them small and outside the usable basket floor; no handle may cross the interior. No handles at top or bottom. Preserve the original basket body dimensions and placement, rim, inner walls, large open woven floor, perspective, coarse pixel art, honey-brown palette, lighting, dark olive backdrop, and landscape 1672x941 composition. Do not shrink, move, rotate, or redesign the basket body or floor to make room. Change only the handles and their immediate background. No apples, people, props, text, UI, watermark, blur, or photorealistic detail. Opaque background.

Generation prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: background for a playable top-down 2D pixel-art apple-dodging game. Create a landscape 16:9 image, ideally 1280x720. The camera looks down INSIDE ONE LARGE EMPTY APPLE-PICKING BASKET. The player will be tiny inside it. Natural golden honey-brown wicker basket, rectangular with softly clipped/rounded corners, a thick braided rim, visible inner walls and a broad flat woven bottom. Basket occupies most of the canvas. Exact layout: entire basket outer rim approximately x=8%-92%, y=13%-94% of canvas; playable inner bottom approximately x=16%-84%, y=27%-81%, rounded/clipped corners; bottom/front rim thick enough to feel deep. A simple curved wicker carrying handle arches behind the back/top rim, near y=4%-16%, without crossing the playable floor. Surrounding backdrop plain dark muted olive green. Empty interior: no apples, no player, no objects, no grass, no path, no signs, no text, no icons, no UI. Crisp hand-pixelled game art with a consistent coarse square pixel grid comparable to a 320x180 scene enlarged with nearest-neighbor, dark brown outlines, limited warm ochre and tan palette, clustered pixel shading, highlights from upper left. Show recognizable over-under wicker weave but make the floor subtly textured, LOW CONTRAST and medium-light tan, so black falling-object shadows will be very easy to see. Darker inner walls and thick braided edging clearly delineate the playable floor. The basket floor must be a large open usable rectangular arena; gentle three-quarter top-down perspective, no deep perspective foreshortening, no isometric diamond, no perspective vanishing point. No blur, no realistic photographs, no smooth vector gradients, no decorative panels, no drop shadows on the middle floor. Output a complete background ready to place behind sprites.
